NOTES prints the tunnel route table on the root host only:
  1: |
    |
      Your release "svc" (chart your-service-name 0.1.0)
      has been installed into namespace "app".

        environment : dev
        db namespace: app-db
        database    : in-cluster PostgreSQL (svc-your-service-name-postgresql.app-db.svc.cluster.local)

      Verify the rollout:
        kubectl -n app get pods -l app.kubernetes.io/instance=svc
        kubectl -n app get job svc-your-service-name-migrate-r0   # this revision's migration Job

      Edge mode "tunnel": no Ingress or HTTPRoute is rendered. Add one published route per line below to
      the tunnel (hostname, path, service URL; see the edge docs in wiki/infrastructure.md).
      The path is the regular expression cloudflared matches (anchored here: it is unanchored otherwise);
      (empty) is the catch-all. Routes match in order and the first match wins, so keep each host's lines in
      this order, the catch-all last, and create the host's Access application first.
      Cloudflare terminates TLS for the public hostnames; the hop from cloudflared to the Service is http:
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        ^/api(/|$)               http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        ^/docs(/|$)              http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        ^/openapi\.json$         http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        (empty)                  http://svc-your-service-name-frontend.app.svc.cluster.local:3000

      Port-forward the backend API locally:
        kubectl -n app port-forward svc/svc-your-service-name-backend 8000:8000
        curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/healthz
an api host adds the backend routes on it, and no frontend route:
  1: |
    |
      Your release "svc" (chart your-service-name 0.1.0)
      has been installed into namespace "app".

        environment : dev
        db namespace: app-db
        database    : in-cluster PostgreSQL (svc-your-service-name-postgresql.app-db.svc.cluster.local)

      Verify the rollout:
        kubectl -n app get pods -l app.kubernetes.io/instance=svc
        kubectl -n app get job svc-your-service-name-migrate-r0   # this revision's migration Job

      Edge mode "tunnel": no Ingress or HTTPRoute is rendered. Add one published route per line below to
      the tunnel (hostname, path, service URL; see the edge docs in wiki/infrastructure.md).
      The path is the regular expression cloudflared matches (anchored here: it is unanchored otherwise);
      (empty) is the catch-all. Routes match in order and the first match wins, so keep each host's lines in
      this order, the catch-all last, and create the host's Access application first.
      Cloudflare terminates TLS for the public hostnames; the hop from cloudflared to the Service is http:
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        ^/api(/|$)               http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        ^/docs(/|$)              http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        ^/openapi\.json$         http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        your-service-name.your-domain.example        (empty)                  http://svc-your-service-name-frontend.app.svc.cluster.local:3000
        svc-api.example.org                          ^/api(/|$)               http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        svc-api.example.org                          ^/docs(/|$)              http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000
        svc-api.example.org                          ^/openapi\.json$         http://svc-your-service-name-backend.app.svc.cluster.local:8000

      Port-forward the backend API locally:
        kubectl -n app port-forward svc/svc-your-service-name-backend 8000:8000
        curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/healthz
